@startuml
title ioScope Scenario View - FTDI Read, Tee to File, and Live Refresh
autonumber

actor User
participant ioQtScopeWindow as Window
participant ioOscilloscopeController as Controller
participant ioLiveOscilloscopeSession as LiveSession
participant ioPipelineController as PipelineController
participant ioUsbReadController as Reader
participant ioTappedReadableByteStream as Tapped
participant ioLiveSampleHistory as History
participant ioDataBuffer as Buffer
participant ioUsbWriteController as Writer
participant ioFileByteStream as FileOut
participant ioOscilloscopeModel as Model
participant ioFilterPipeline as Pipeline
participant ioCompactOscilloscopeView as Compact
participant ioDetailedOscilloscopeView as Detailed

loop while session is running
  Reader -> Tapped : read_bytes(chunk)
  Tapped -> History : append_bytes(payload)
  Reader -> Buffer : push(payload)
  Writer -> Buffer : pop(chunk)
  Writer -> FileOut : write_bytes(payload)

  Window -> Controller : refreshLiveSession()
  Controller -> LiveSession : latest_samples(limit)
  LiveSession -> History : latest_samples(limit)
  History --> LiveSession : normalized samples
  LiveSession --> Controller : latest samples
  Controller -> Model : setRawSignal(samples)
  Model -> Pipeline : process(raw signal)
  Pipeline --> Model : processed signal
  Controller -> Compact : render(ioRenderState)
  Controller -> Detailed : render(ioRenderState)
  Window -> Window : show active concrete view instance
end

User -> Window : click Stop
Window -> Controller : stop()
Controller -> LiveSession : stop()
LiveSession -> PipelineController : stop()
PipelineController -> Buffer : close()
Controller -> Model : appendEvent("session_stop")

note over Reader, FileOut
Incoming FTDI bytes are mirrored in two directions:
into sample history for the waveform and into the tee-output
file through the shared circular-buffer pipeline.
end note
@enduml
